WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:16,390
My naturopathic doctor recently commented that the only scan available that truly identifies

00:00:16,390 --> 00:00:24,390
a truer tuber as biologically active in a living cancer cell is a pet scan.

00:00:24,390 --> 00:00:28,230
All other scans, including the Pradovo, just detect a mass.

00:00:28,230 --> 00:00:34,390
We assume, obviously, if the size is growing, that's an active cancer, but if we've got a

00:00:34,390 --> 00:00:40,830
lump that's really staying the same size, there's no way to know if it's a brotic tissue or

00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:42,830
cancer or something else.

00:00:42,830 --> 00:00:47,150
Do I agree?

00:00:47,150 --> 00:00:54,430
The answer that is yes, I do agree, and I'll go even one step further just because it's

00:00:54,430 --> 00:01:00,470
showing up as metabolically active on a pet scan doesn't mean it's necessarily growing.

00:01:00,470 --> 00:01:06,110
So any living tissue is going to have metabolic activity.

00:01:06,110 --> 00:01:10,430
What a pet scan's looking for is that difference in metabolic activity.

00:01:10,430 --> 00:01:17,430
Is it highly metabolic that's going to, as they tune their instrument, you know, they're

00:01:17,430 --> 00:01:22,270
looking for where there's higher metabolic activity in an area.

00:01:22,270 --> 00:01:28,790
So yes, I would totally agree that a pet scan is the only way to show and to scan what

00:01:28,790 --> 00:01:31,350
is metabolically active.

00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:34,030
Everything else is going to look at a mass.

00:01:34,030 --> 00:01:38,150
They can't look at whether it's living tissue, growing tissue, or anything else, but a pet

00:01:38,150 --> 00:01:41,510
scan still can't even say that it's growing.

00:01:41,510 --> 00:01:50,310
So if you really want to know if there's cancer in other places, a pet scan is really the best

00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:51,310
scan.

00:01:51,310 --> 00:01:56,590
Now, the reason why a person would choose the Pradovo over a pet scan is simply because of

00:01:56,590 --> 00:01:59,710
the radiation issue with a pet scan.

00:01:59,710 --> 00:02:05,150
You're getting radiation and you're having to take a sugar dose with a pet scan and some

00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:08,750
people are opposed to doing that and understandable.

00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:11,790
So you just have to weigh it out what you're really looking for.

00:02:11,790 --> 00:02:16,110
If you know you have cancer and you know what's active and you just want to know if you have

00:02:16,110 --> 00:02:23,310
cancer somewhere else, doing a Pradovo is the least invasive of those.

00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:30,510
And if you haven't had a lot of pet scans, you haven't had a lot of CT scans, then you

00:02:30,510 --> 00:02:41,150
know getting a pet scan done is more accurate, I would say, but it comes with it the invasiveness

00:02:41,150 --> 00:02:45,470
of the radiation and the invasiveness of having to take the glucose syrup.

00:02:45,470 --> 00:02:48,590
So that's where people go against it.

00:02:48,590 --> 00:02:54,630
But again, remember all those things, it's the radiation is what's measured and what's

00:02:54,630 --> 00:02:56,790
called a rad dose.

00:02:56,790 --> 00:03:00,470
The more radiation that you get throughout your lifetime, the more damaging it's going to

00:03:00,470 --> 00:03:01,470
be.

00:03:01,470 --> 00:03:06,870
So if you're like, all I've got is dental X-rays and maybe some X-rays at my chiropractor

00:03:06,870 --> 00:03:13,590
and I got an MRI to diagnose my cancer, I haven't even had a pet scan or CT scan.

00:03:13,590 --> 00:03:22,630
But now, you know, I have some bone pain or you have suspect of metastasis, then you

00:03:22,630 --> 00:03:24,670
know go ahead and do a pet scan.

00:03:24,670 --> 00:03:33,870
If you're simply using the pet scan and doing a test just on a curiosity to see if there's

00:03:33,870 --> 00:03:38,910
metabolic activity and things are growing, then I would question that.

00:03:38,910 --> 00:03:46,750
Remember, my whole saying about doing an invasive test is you do an invasive test if it's going

00:03:46,750 --> 00:03:50,030
to change the way you treat the patient.

00:03:50,030 --> 00:03:54,110
So as you as a patient, you would choose to do an invasive test.

00:03:54,110 --> 00:03:57,270
If you're going to choose to change the way you treat it, if you're going to go, if you're

00:03:57,270 --> 00:04:04,390
saying, I'm just curious if the cancer in my breast is is metabolically active and growing,

00:04:04,390 --> 00:04:06,030
I'm not going to do anything different.

00:04:06,030 --> 00:04:10,110
But I'm going to keep doing what I'm doing, then I wouldn't do it.

00:04:10,110 --> 00:04:14,910
But if it's like, okay, I have this horrible pain in my spine and I want to make sure that

00:04:14,910 --> 00:04:23,150
I don't have metastasis to the spine and if I did, I might opt to do radiation or something

00:04:23,150 --> 00:04:25,310
because this has really bothered me.

00:04:25,310 --> 00:04:29,630
Well then that's a reason to do a pet scan because it may change the way you treat it.

